## About

I'm an engineering team lead at Bloomberg. My background is in C++, Python,
Java, distributed systems, and financial analytics.

I’m a limited partner at Oxonian Ventures, investing in startups founded by
Oxford alumni. I’m also on the board of One for the World, helping make
decisions about the charity and its work on effective giving.

I studied mathematics and computer science at Oxford, where I worked on
computational group theory. I also once quit my job to start a VPN business.
I built the product, handled sales and customer service, and spent most of my
time arguing with people on Twitter.

I’ve been writing this blog since 2013. Much of it is about programming,
mathematics, Unix, and getting old computers to do things. More recently,
I’ve been writing about AI, management, and how organisations work. There
are also occasional posts about startups, games, books, and whatever else
has caught my attention.

You can find me on [GitHub](https://github.com/kaashif) and
[LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/in/kaashif-hymabaccus/), or
[get in touch](/contact.html).
